---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;

const pageTitle = "GOTS Certification Explained | What It Means for Your Fas...";
const pageDescription = "Plain English guide to GOTS certification for fashion brands. Learn what it means, requirements, benefits, and how to get certified."
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>

  <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{JSON.stringify({
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": "GOTS Certification Explained | Complete Guide for Fashion Brands",
    "description": pageDescription,
    "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "SDF Clothing" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "SDF Clothing", "url": "https://sdfltd.com" },
    "url": Astro.url.href
  })}</script>

  <div class="container" style="padding: 3rem 1.5rem 5rem;">

    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <p style="font-size: 0.72rem; color: #FFFFFF; letter-spacing: 0.1em; text-transform: uppercase;">
        <a href="/" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">Home</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem; color: #333;"> | </span>
        <a href="/insights/index" style="color: #aaa; text-decoration: none;">Insights</a>
        <span style="margin: 0 0.5rem; color: #333;"> | </span>
        <span style="color: #FFFFFF;">GOTS Certification Explained</span>
      </p>
    </nav>

    <article>

      <header style="max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 3rem; padding-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a;">
        <span style="font-size: 0.62rem; letter-spacing: 0.25em; text-transform: uppercase; color: #e00; display: block; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Sustainability Guide</span>
        <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); font-weight: 200; color: #fff; line-height: 1.2; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: 0.01em;">
          GOTS Certification Explained | What It Means for Your Fashion Brand
        </h1>
        <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #aaa; line-height: 1.9; margin: 0;">
          GOTS stands for Global Organic Textile Standard. It is the world's leading certification for organic textiles. If your fashion brand wants to use the word "organic" on your garments or marketing in the EU, UK, or USA, you need GOTS-certified production.
        </p>
      </header>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">What Does GOTS Certification Mean?</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">GOTS certifies the entire production chain of an organic textile | from raw cotton farm to finished garment. Ecological criteria: prohibits toxic dyes, bleaches, chemicals. Requires wastewater treatment. Bans hazardous substances. Social criteria: requires fair wages, safe working conditions, no child or forced labor, right to collective bargaining.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">Why Does GOTS Matter?</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Legal requirements: EU requires certification for organic claims. Retailer requirements: major retailers like H&M, ASOS, Next require GOTS for organic lines. Consumer trust: eco-conscious consumers check for GOTS certification before buying.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">GOTS vs OEKO-TEX</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">GOTS certifies the entire organic supply chain | fiber origin, processing, labor. OEKO-TEX tests finished garments for harmful substances. OEKO-TEX does not certify organic fiber. For organic claims, GOTS is required. For safety claims, OEKO-TEX is sufficient.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">How to Verify GOTS</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Verify at GOTS.org using certificate number or factory name. Never accept certificates without verification. Fake or expired certificates exist. You receive a Transaction Certificate (TC) for your specific order | this is your proof of GOTS certification for retailers and regulators.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">What Does GOTS Cost?</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Organic cotton costs 20-40% more than conventional. Certification adds cost through audits and fees. Price premium for brands is typically 15-30% above conventional. A $3.50 conventional t-shirt might cost $4.20-4.50 GOTS organic.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase">Which Markets Require GOTS?</h2>
      <div style="background: #050505; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; border-left: 0.6px solid #e00; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;"><strong style="color: #fff;">EU:</strong> Ecodesign regulation makes GOTS important for organic claims.</p>
        <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;"><strong style="color: #fff;">UK:</strong> Retailers require GOTS for organic ranges. ASA requires substantiated proof.</p>
        <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;"><strong style="color: #fff;">USA:</strong> GOTS is recognized as the credible organic textile standard.</p>
        <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0;"><strong style="color: #fff;">Australia:</strong> ACCC requires substantiated proof for organic claims.</p>
      </div>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">How to Order GOTS Garments</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Confirm factory holds current GOTS certificate (verify on GOTS.org). Specify GOTS organic fabric in your order. Factory sources from certified mills with tracked certification. You receive Transaction Certificate for your order | this is your legal documentation for organic claims.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 400; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; color: #fff; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase;">GOTS vs OCS</h2>
      <p style="color: #aaa; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 0.95rem; margin-bottom: 3rem;">OCS certifies organic fiber content only. GOTS covers entire production chain and includes social criteria. GOTS is more rigorous and carries more credibility. For retailer and regulator organic claims, GOTS is the stronger choice.</p>

      <div style="text-align: center; padding: 2.5rem; border: 1px solid #1a1a1a; border-top: 0.6px solid #e00; background: #050505; margin-top: 3rem;">
        <p style="color: #fff; font-size: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; font-weight: 300;">
          Want to launch an organic clothing line with GOTS-certified production? Contact SDF Clothing. We are GOTS certified and produce organic cotton garments from 300 pieces per style. We provide Transaction Certificates with every GOTS order.
        </p>
        <a href="/contact" style="display: inline-block; background: #e00; color: #fff; padding: 0.9rem 2.5rem; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.15em; text-transform: uppercase; transition: background 0.2s;">
          Contact Us ?
        </a>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #aaa; margin-top: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.8;">
        For a complete overview of clothing manufacturers in Bangladesh | including factory types, MOQ ranges, certifications, and sourcing guide | read our <a href="/clothing-manufacturers" style="color: #e00; text-decoration: none;">complete clothing manufacturers guide</a>.
      </p>

      <p style="font-size:0.85rem; color:#aaa; margin-top:1.75rem; line-height:1.85;">
        For a complete overview of clothing manufacturers in Bangladesh | including factory types, MOQ ranges, certifications, sourcing methods, and product categories | read our <a href="/clothing-manufacturers" style="color:#e00; text-decoration:none;">complete clothing manufacturers guide</a>.
      </p>

    </article>

  </div>

    
    </BaseLayout>




